  "description": "Motorcycle powertrain integration: engine configurations (single, parallel-twin, inline-four, V-twin, boxer), sequential constant-mesh gearbox, wet multi-plate clutch, and final drive systems (chain, belt, shaft). Covers power delivery characteristics, gearing for varied top speed versus acceleration tradeoffs, and electric motorcycle powertrains using hub motors or mid-drive motors with single-speed reduction. Builds on internal-combustion engine and electric motor capabilities without duplicating their fundamentals.",
